# .scoutignore — Docker Scout CVEs reviewed and accepted (blessed) as
# currently unfixable. Applied to Scout's own report by `build` Stage 4c
# (Scout has no native ignorefile, unlike Trivy's --ignorefile or Grype's
# --config). One CVE/GHSA id per line; '#' starts a comment.
#
# Every entry here is documented in SECURITY.md, including why it has no
# installable fix today. Unlike `.scout.vex.json` (reserved for verified
# false positives — a VEX `not_affected` statement asserts the finding
# does not apply at all), these are genuine, currently-present findings
# that this project has reviewed and chosen not to block the build on.
# Review this list whenever `aws-backup-base` is bumped or the AL2023
# repository gains a newer python3-urllib3/python3-setuptools build —
# the fix may already exist upstream even though Scout still reports it.
#
# Added 2026-11-24, verified against the aws-backup-base 1.2.3 pin.

# urllib3 (RPM python3-urllib3 1.25.10): no AL2023 RPM fix; awscli-2 pins
# python3.9dist(urllib3) <= 2.6.3, so the RPM cannot be upgraded or removed.
CVE-2021-33503
CVE-2023-43804
CVE-2025-66418
CVE-2025-66471
CVE-2026-21441

# urllib3 (RPM 1.25.10 and pip-installed 2.6.3, both affected): the next
# urllib3 releases (2.7.0, 2.8.0) declare requires_python ">=3.10"; the
# base image ships Python 3.9.
CVE-2026-44431
CVE-2026-44432
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689

# setuptools (RPM python3-setuptools 59.6.0): no AL2023 RPM fix;
# python3-ruamel-yaml and python3-distro (both awscli-2 dependencies)
# require it.
CVE-2022-40897
CVE-2024-6345
CVE-2025-47273
